    {
      "block_id": "2605.18130_p12_b55",
      "text": "Fig. 5: Cross-correlation heatmap between explicit radiomic\npriors and implicit deep representations. The analysis illus-\ntrates a moderate yet significant semantic alignment, highlight-\ning the feature complementarity of the dual-branch framework.\n",
      "bbox": [
        48.96,
        523.46,
        300.02,
        569.29
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        195,
        2093,
        1200,
        2277
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 248,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.18130_p12_b56",
      "text": "network does not merely memorize abstract noise; rather, it\nimplicitly encodes meaningful clinical phenotypes analogous\nto traditional heterogeneity metrics. Crucially, the moderate\nmagnitude of these correlations demonstrates that the two\nfeature spaces are fundamentally complementary rather than\nredundant. While the deep branch captures high-order, non-\nlinear topological patterns, the radiomic pathway explicitly\nanchors the diagnostic reasoning with robust, physically in-\nterpretable constraints. Ultimately, this dual-stream synergy\nstrongly supports the necessity of our proposed architecture\nin providing complementary information sources and bridging\nthe gap between deep feature efficacy and clinical trust.\n",
      "bbox": [
        48.96,
        606.82,
        300.02,
        748.29
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        195,
        2427,
        1200,
